# PR #1188 runs this gate in lane 3 of the parallel `lint` matrix. The six
# filters run in one `cargo test` instead of six chained ones, since libtest
# ORs its filters, so the same tests run once. Main run 36292106539 showed
# each of the six invocations recompiling formal-ai, about 90s apiece of the
# gate's 604s.
ci_gate repository_workspace_protocol
  stage rust
  lane 3
  description "The repository workspace stays one exact-commit, default-deny protocol: clone/diff isolation, multilingual target location, named-test evidence, data/source grounding and solve attribution are exercised together so a caller cannot bypass a protocol step unnoticed."
  run "cargo test --manifest-path rust/Cargo.toml --locked --test unit -- issue_1138_repository_workspace issue_1138_locate_targets issue_1138_named_tests repository_workspace_protocol issue_1138_solve_cli solve_commit_payload_is_accepted_by_the_canonical_attribution_parser"
  justification "A caller that bypasses a protocol step (clone isolation, attribution, data grounding) can silently produce commits that fail the self-hosting metric; the protocol tests were introduced in #1138 (commit 9c31b0530) to make every bypass visible."
